                       {'id': '4ed3c6b8-e548-4aee-b96d-9f4ce8c650ff',
                        'name': '18e3 Clean background',
                        'type': 'n8n-nodes-base.code',
                        'typeVersion': 2,
                        'alwaysOutputData': True,
                        'onError': 'continueRegularOutput',
                        'position': [11008, 1360],
                        'parameters': {'jsCode': '// Stage 06 · Clean background (P1.7; owner decision D4, '
                                                 '16 Oct 2026, 11:3x). Code only, no AI, no paid call.\n'
                                                 '// The delivery files only: the approved master in Drive '
                                                 'stays untouched. Input: the master resized to the delivery '
                                                 'size as a BMP\n'
                                                 '// ("pix", made by 18e2 with n8n Edit Image). Output: the '
                                                 'same picture with its background set to 255 ("clean", '
                                                 'BMP), from which\n'
                                                 '// 18f and 18g write the jpg and the webp. 18h then reads '
                                                 'the saved files back and checks that their edge rows read '
                                                 '255.\n'
                                                 "// The owner's conditions:\n"
                                                 '// 1. Reuse the logic of "Claude · Midas white clean-up" '
                                                 '(MSU2K5WKKfizCapW): its background sample from the outer '
                                                 'edge band, its\n'
                                                 '//    near-white test (darkest channel at least 205, '
                                                 'channels within 30), its white point from that sample (the '
                                                 'value under which 5% of\n'
                                                 '//    the near-white pixels lie, minus 2, kept between 228 '
                                                 'and 253) and its soft curve: from the knee (22 below the '
                                                 'white point) up to the\n'
                                                 '//    white point, values rise smoothly to 255; at or '
                                                 'above the white point they become 255. Not reused: its '
                                                 'paid fal.ai cut-out\n'
                                                 '//    (BiRefNet) and its fal storage upload, because this '
                                                 'step uses no AI (the owner\'s "no AI" for the package).\n'
                                                 '// 2. Only background pixels change (fixed 16 Oct 2026 '
                                                 'after the independent review, finding 1):\n'
                                                 '//    - The fill grows from the image border only through '
                                                 'pixels at or above the white point (every channel), so it '
                                                 'never crosses a\n'
                                                 '//      shaded product surface, however soft its edge.\n'
                                                 '//    - The soft curve is applied only to a thin band '
                                                 '(BAND px) around the filled area, so the edge of the fill '
                                                 'blends in.\n'
                                                 "//    - Nothing inside the product's box changes. The box "
                                                 "is the approved review's blind-count box (box_2d, 0-1000), "
                                                 'widened by MARGIN on\n'
                                                 '//      the top, left and right; the strip below it (the '
                                                 'contact shadow) is not widened, so the shadow edge can '
                                                 'still be cleaned. Outside\n'
                                                 '//      the box, changes fade in over RAMP px, so no '
                                                 'box-shaped step shows where background is visible inside '
                                                 'the box.\n'
                                                 '//    - With no usable box from the review, nothing is '
                                                 'changed: the product cannot be protected without it. The '
                                                 'package is still made\n'
                                                 "//      with the master's own background, and the skipped "
                                                 'steps are recorded (owner, 16 Oct 2026, 19:26).\n'
                                                 '//    - Product pixels changed is measured (pixels changed '
                                                 'inside the box), not assumed.\n'
                                                 '// 3. The contact shadow stays: anything darker than the '
                                                 'knee never changes (measured too); the faint edge of the '
                                                 'shadow is lifted only\n'
                                                 '//    along the soft curve, inside the thin band.\n'
                                                 '// 4. The check after saving is in 18h (the saved jpg and '
                                                 'webp, read back).\n'
                                                 '// 5. The manifest notes "background set to 255" (18l).\n'
                                                 "const pk = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify($('18e Check "
                                                 "master').first().json.pk));\n"
                                                 'const item = $input.first() || {};\n'
                                                 'const bin = item.binary || {};\n'
                                                 'const BAND = 3;     // px around the filled background '
                                                 'that get the soft curve (the review asked for 2-3 px)\n'
                                                 'const MARGIN = 15;  // of 1000: the product box is widened '
                                                 "by this on the top, left and right (as the crop rule's "
                                                 'edge limit), not below\n'
                                                 'const RAMP_PCT = 6; // changes fade in over 6% of the '
                                                 "picture's side outside the product box (68 px at 1125), so "
                                                 "the master's own\n"
                                                 '                    // near-white inside the box meets 255 '
                                                 'by a gradient too gentle to see (ASSUMPTION, see README)\n'
                                                 'const GUARD = 8;    // px of fully white background kept '
                                                 'at every image edge, for codec edge blocks\n'
                                                 'const FIT_SPAN_PCT = Number(pk.cfg && pk.cfg.fit_span_pct) '
                                                 '|| 76; // white-master framing setting: the longest side '
                                                 'spans 76% of the frame\n'
                                                 'function bmpInfo(b) {\n'
                                                 '  if (b.length < 54 || b[0] !== 0x42 || b[1] !== 0x4d) '
                                                 "throw new Error('not a BMP file');\n"
                                                 '  const off = b.readUInt32LE(10);\n'
                                                 '  const head = b.readUInt32LE(14);\n'
                                                 '  const w = b.readInt32LE(18);\n'
                                                 '  const rawH = b.readInt32LE(22);\n'
                                                 '  const h = Math.abs(rawH);\n'
                                                 '  const bits = b.readUInt16LE(28);\n'
                                                 '  const comp = b.readUInt32LE(30);\n'
                                                 '  if ((bits !== 24 && bits !== 32) || (comp !== 0 && comp '
                                                 "!== 3)) throw new Error('unsupported BMP: ' + bits + ' "
                                                 "bits, compression ' + comp);\n"
                                                 '  let ri = 2, gi = 1, bi = 0;\n'
                                                 '  if (comp === 3 && bits === 32) {\n'
                                                 '    const at = head >= 52 ? 54 : 14 + head;\n'
                                                 '    const byteOf = mask => (mask === 0xff ? 0 : (mask === '
                                                 '0xff00 ? 1 : (mask === 0xff0000 ? 2 : 3)));\n'
                                                 '    ri = byteOf(b.readUInt32LE(at)); gi = '
                                                 'byteOf(b.readUInt32LE(at + 4)); bi = '
                                                 'byteOf(b.readUInt32LE(at + 8));\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  const stride = Math.floor((bits * w + 31) / 32) * 4;\n'
                                                 '  if (w < 8 || h < 8 || off + stride * h > b.length) throw '
                                                 "new Error('BMP size does not match its header');\n"
                                                 '  return { w, h, bytes: bits / 8, off, stride, bottomUp: '
                                                 'rawH > 0, ri, gi, bi };\n'
                                                 '}\n'
                                                 'function boxOf(v) {\n'
                                                 '  const b = Array.isArray(v) ? v.map(Number) : [];\n'
                                                 '  return b.length === 4 && b.every(x => Number.isFinite(x) '
                                                 '&& x >= 0 && x <= 1000) && b[0] < b[2] && b[1] < b[3] && '
                                                 '!b.every(x => x <= 1) ? b : null;\n'
                                                 '}\n'
                                                 "const wc = { done: false, method: 'background set to 255 "
                                                 'in code (no AI): a fill from the image border through '
                                                 'pixels at or above the white point only, the soft curve of '
                                                 "the white clean-up workflow on a ' + BAND + ' px band "
                                                 'around it, nothing changed inside the product box from the '
                                                 'review; the contact shadow and the product are not changed '
                                                 "(measured)', band_px: BAND, box_margin_of_1000: MARGIN, "
                                                 'ramp_pct: RAMP_PCT };\n'
                                                 'let cleanBin = null;\n'
                                                 'const SKIP = { skip: true };\n'
                                                 '// Owner, 16 Oct 2026, 19:26 (Phase 1 question 1): with no '
                                                 'product box the master is still packaged, but the '
                                                 'background is NOT cleaned\n'
                                                 "// (the clean-up could eat into a white or cream product's "
                                                 "edges without the box). The master's own background is "
                                                 'delivered and the\n'
                                                 "// skip is recorded; 18h measures the saved files' edges "
                                                 'and reports them, without the 255 rule. Every step that '
                                                 'needs the box is listed.\n'
                                                 'const SKIPPED_NO_BOX = [\n'
                                                 "  { step: 'background set to 255 (the clean-up and its "
                                                 "fade around the product)', why: 'it needs the product box, "
                                                 "so the product\\'s edges are not touched without it' },\n"
                                                 "  { step: 'framing band check (white master 72-80% on the "
                                                 "longest side)', why: 'it needs the product box; not "
                                                 "measured' }\n"
                                                 '];\n'
                                                 'try {\n'
                                                 '  let box = boxOf(pk.product_box_2d);\n'
                                                 '  wc.product_box_2d = box;\n'
                                                 "  if (!bin.pix) throw new Error('the master could not be "
                                                 "turned into pixels (Edit Image gave no BMP' + (item.json "
                                                 "&& item.json.error ? ': ' + String(item.json.error.message "
                                                 "|| item.json.error).slice(0, 160) : '') + ')');\n"
                                                 '  const b = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(0, '
                                                 "'pix');\n"
                                                 '  const m = bmpInfo(b);\n'
                                                 '  const w = m.w, h = m.h, N = w * h;\n'
                                                 '  if (w !== pk.cfg.size_px || h !== pk.cfg.size_px) throw '
                                                 "new Error('the pixels are ' + w + ' x ' + h + ', not ' + "
                                                 "pk.cfg.size_px + ' x ' + pk.cfg.size_px);\n"
                                                 '  if (!box) {\n'
                                                 '    wc.skipped = true; wc.done = false; wc.cleaned = '
                                                 'false;\n'
                                                 "    wc.skip_reason = 'no usable product box (box_2d) from "
                                                 "the review';\n"
                                                 '    wc.skipped_steps = SKIPPED_NO_BOX;\n'
                                                 "    wc.method = 'background not cleaned: no product box "
                                                 "from the review, so the master\\'s own background is "
                                                 "delivered unchanged';\n"
                                                 '    cleanBin = await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(b, '
                                                 "pk.base + '_clean.bmp', 'image/bmp');\n"
                                                 '    throw SKIP; // leaves the try block: nothing below '
                                                 'runs; the picture goes on unchanged\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  const R = new Uint8Array(N), G = new Uint8Array(N), B = '
                                                 'new Uint8Array(N);\n'
                                                 '  for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) {\n'
                                                 '    const base = m.off + (m.bottomUp ? h - 1 - y : y) * '
                                                 'm.stride;\n'
                                                 '    for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) { const p = base + x * '
                                                 'm.bytes, i = y * w + x; R[i] = b[p + m.ri]; G[i] = b[p + '
                                                 'm.gi]; B[i] = b[p + m.bi]; }\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  // 1. The background sample from the outer edge band (as '
                                                 "the white clean-up's C9 does).\n"
                                                 '  const band = Math.max(2, Math.round(0.04 * Math.min(w, '
                                                 'h)));\n'
                                                 '  const hist = [new Uint32Array(256), new '
                                                 'Uint32Array(256), new Uint32Array(256)];\n'
                                                 '  let seen = 0, whitish = 0;\n'
                                                 '  for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) '
                                                 '{\n'
                                                 '    if (!(y < band || y >= h - band || x < band || x >= w '
                                                 '- band)) continue;\n'
                                                 '    const i = y * w + x, hi = Math.max(R[i], G[i], B[i]), '
                                                 'lo = Math.min(R[i], G[i], B[i]);\n'
                                                 '    seen++;\n'
                                                 '    if (lo >= 205 && hi - lo <= 30) { whitish++; '
                                                 'hist[0][R[i]]++; hist[1][G[i]]++; hist[2][B[i]]++; }\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  const whiteShare = seen ? Math.round(1000 * whitish / '
                                                 'seen) / 10 : 0;\n'
                                                 '  wc.edge_band_near_white_pct = whiteShare;\n'
                                                 "  if (whiteShare < 50) throw new Error('the edge of the "
                                                 "master is not near-white (' + whiteShare + '% of it), so "
                                                 "its background was left as it is');\n"
                                                 '  const top = [0, 0, 0], knee = [0, 0, 0], lut = [new '
                                                 'Uint8Array(256), new Uint8Array(256), new '
                                                 'Uint8Array(256)];\n'
                                                 '  for (let c = 0; c < 3; c++) {\n'
                                                 '    let acc = 0, v = 205;\n'
                                                 '    while (v < 255 && acc + hist[c][v] < 0.05 * whitish) { '
                                                 'acc += hist[c][v]; v += 1; }\n'
                                                 '    top[c] = Math.max(228, Math.min(253, v - 2));\n'
                                                 '    knee[c] = top[c] - 22;\n'
                                                 '    for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) lut[c][i] = i >= top[c] '
                                                 '? 255 : (i > knee[c] ? Math.round(knee[c] + (i - knee[c]) '
                                                 '* (255 - knee[c]) / (top[c] - knee[c])) : i);\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  const kneeMin = Math.min(knee[0], knee[1], knee[2]);\n'
                                                 '  wc.white_from = top; wc.curve_starts_at = knee;\n'
                                                 '  // 1b. Fit (owner, 20 Oct 2026, run claude-a7-4f80c2bf): '
                                                 'a master framed so tight that the protected box leaves no '
                                                 'safe margin at an\n'
                                                 '  //     image edge used to hold the package. It is now '
                                                 'placed on a white canvas in code: scaled down (never up) '
                                                 "so the product's longest\n"
                                                 '  //     side spans the white-master framing setting '
                                                 '(FIT_SPAN_PCT), and the product box centred. No AI, '
                                                 'nothing redrawn: the picture is\n'
                                                 '  //     resampled once more (bilinear), like the resize '
                                                 'before it, and the new canvas is 255. The white point '
                                                 'above was read from the\n'
                                                 "  //     master's own edge before the canvas is added, so "
                                                 "the fill still reaches the master's own background. Only a "
                                                 'master that would\n'
                                                 '  //     otherwise hold is fitted; any other keeps its '
                                                 'framing.\n'
                                                 '  const boxPx = bx => {\n'
                                                 '    const mg0 = MARGIN / 1000;\n'
                                                 '    return [Math.max(0, Math.floor((bx[1] / 1000 - mg0) * '
                                                 'w)), Math.max(0, Math.floor((bx[0] / 1000 - mg0) * h)),\n'
                                                 '      Math.min(w - 1, Math.ceil((bx[3] / 1000 + mg0) * '
                                                 'w)), Math.min(h - 1, Math.ceil(bx[2] / 1000 * h))];\n'
                                                 '  };\n'
                                                 '  const unsafe = bx => { const p = boxPx(bx); return '
                                                 'Math.min(p[0], w - 1 - p[2], p[1], h - 1 - p[3]) <= GUARD; '
                                                 '};\n'
                                                 '  if (unsafe(box)) {\n'
                                                 '    const spanBefore = Math.max(box[3] - box[1], box[2] - '
                                                 'box[0]) / 10;\n'
                                                 '    const s = Math.min(1, FIT_SPAN_PCT / spanBefore);\n'
                                                 '    const cx = (box[1] + box[3]) / 2000 * w, cy = (box[0] '
                                                 '+ box[2]) / 2000 * h;\n'
                                                 '    const R2 = new Uint8Array(N), G2 = new Uint8Array(N), '
                                                 'B2 = new Uint8Array(N);\n'
                                                 '    for (let Y = 0; Y < h; Y++) for (let X = 0; X < w; '
                                                 'X++) {\n'
                                                 '      const o = Y * w + X;\n'
                                                 '      const sx = cx + (X + 0.5 - w / 2) / s - 0.5, sy = cy '
                                                 '+ (Y + 0.5 - h / 2) / s - 0.5;\n'
                                                 '      if (sx < -0.5 || sy < -0.5 || sx > w - 0.5 || sy > h '
                                                 '- 0.5) { R2[o] = 255; G2[o] = 255; B2[o] = 255; continue; '
                                                 '}\n'
                                                 '      const x0 = Math.max(0, Math.min(w - 1, '
                                                 'Math.floor(sx))), y0 = Math.max(0, Math.min(h - 1, '
                                                 'Math.floor(sy)));\n'
                                                 '      const x1 = Math.min(w - 1, x0 + 1), y1 = Math.min(h '
                                                 '- 1, y0 + 1);\n'
                                                 '      const fx = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, sx - x0)), fy = '
                                                 'Math.max(0, Math.min(1, sy - y0));\n'
                                                 '      const a = y0 * w + x0, b1 = y0 * w + x1, c = y1 * w '
                                                 '+ x0, d = y1 * w + x1;\n'
                                                 '      const mix = A => Math.round((A[a] * (1 - fx) + A[b1] '
                                                 '* fx) * (1 - fy) + (A[c] * (1 - fx) + A[d] * fx) * fy);\n'
                                                 '      R2[o] = mix(R); G2[o] = mix(G); B2[o] = mix(B);\n'
                                                 '    }\n'
                                                 '    R.set(R2); G.set(G2); B.set(B2);\n'
                                                 '    const to1000 = (v, side, c0) => Math.round(((v / 1000 '
                                                 '* side - c0) * s + side / 2) / side * 1000);\n'
                                                 '    const fitted = [to1000(box[0], h, cy), to1000(box[1], '
                                                 'w, cx), to1000(box[2], h, cy), to1000(box[3], w, cx)];\n'
                                                 "    wc.fit = { done: true, why: 'the product box left no "
                                                 "safe background margin at an image edge', scale: "
                                                 'Math.round(s * 1000) / 1000,\n'
                                                 '      span_before_pct: Math.round(spanBefore * 10) / 10, '
                                                 'span_after_pct: Math.round(spanBefore * s * 10) / 10, '
                                                 'target_span_pct: FIT_SPAN_PCT,\n'
                                                 '      box_2d_before: box, box_2d_after: fitted,\n'
                                                 "      method: 'scaled by ' + (Math.round(s * 1000) / 1000) "
                                                 "+ ' (bilinear) and centred on a white (255) canvas in "
                                                 "code; no AI, nothing redrawn' };\n"
                                                 '    box = fitted;\n'
                                                 '    wc.product_box_2d = box;\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  // 2. The product box in pixels: widened by MARGIN on '
                                                 'the top, left and right; the bottom edge (the contact '
                                                 'shadow side) is not widened.\n'
                                                 '  const RAMP = Math.max(8, Math.round(RAMP_PCT / 100 * '
                                                 'Math.min(w, h)));\n'
                                                 '  wc.ramp_px = RAMP;\n'
                                                 '  const mg = MARGIN / 1000;\n'
                                                 '  const bx0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((box[1] / 1000 - mg) '
                                                 '* w)), bx1 = Math.min(w - 1, Math.ceil((box[3] / 1000 + '
                                                 'mg) * w));\n'
                                                 '  const by0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((box[0] / 1000 - mg) '
                                                 '* h)), by1 = Math.min(h - 1, Math.ceil(box[2] / 1000 * '
                                                 'h));\n'
                                                 '  wc.product_box_px = [bx0, by0, bx1, by1];\n'
                                                 '  const inBox = (x, y) => x >= bx0 && x <= bx1 && y >= by0 '
                                                 '&& y <= by1;\n'
                                                 '  // Fit the fade to each available margin. A fixed 68 px '
                                                 'fade left narrow borders\n'
                                                 '  // unfinished. Keep eight fully white background pixels '
                                                 'for codec edge blocks.\n'
                                                 '  const guard = GUARD;\n'
                                                 '  const gaps = { left: bx0, right: w - 1 - bx1, top: by0, '
                                                 'bottom: h - 1 - by1 };\n'
                                                 '  if (Object.values(gaps).some(v => v <= guard)) throw new '
                                                 "Error('the protected product box leaves no safe background "
                                                 "margin at an image edge');\n"
                                                 '  const ramps = '
                                                 'Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(gaps).map(([k, v]) => '
                                                 '[k, Math.min(RAMP, v - guard)]));\n'
                                                 '  wc.edge_guard_px = guard; wc.side_ramps_px = ramps;\n'
                                                 '  // None inside the box; every fade finishes before the '
                                                 'codec edge band.\n'
                                                 '  const weight = (x, y) => {\n'
                                                 '    const dx = x < bx0 ? (bx0 - x) / ramps.left : (x > bx1 '
                                                 '? (x - bx1) / ramps.right : 0);\n'
                                                 '    const dy = y < by0 ? (by0 - y) / ramps.top : (y > by1 '
                                                 '? (y - by1) / ramps.bottom : 0);\n'
                                                 '    return Math.min(1, Math.hypot(dx, dy));\n'
                                                 '  };\n'
                                                 '  // 3. The fill from the border, only through pixels at '
                                                 'or above the white point (every channel), never into the '
                                                 'box.\n'
                                                 '  const white = i => R[i] >= top[0] && G[i] >= top[1] && '
                                                 'B[i] >= top[2];\n'
                                                 '  const region = new Uint8Array(N);\n'
                                                 '  const stack = new Int32Array(N);\n'
                                                 '  let sp = 0;\n'
                                                 '  const tryAdd = (i, x, y) => { if (!region[i] && '
                                                 '!inBox(x, y) && white(i)) { region[i] = 1; stack[sp++] = '
                                                 'i; } };\n'
                                                 '  for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) { tryAdd(x, x, 0); tryAdd((h '
                                                 '- 1) * w + x, x, h - 1); }\n'
                                                 '  for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) { tryAdd(y * w, 0, y); '
                                                 'tryAdd(y * w + w - 1, w - 1, y); }\n'
                                                 '  while (sp) {\n'
                                                 '    const i = stack[--sp], x = i % w, y = (i - x) / w;\n'
                                                 '    if (x > 0) tryAdd(i - 1, x - 1, y);\n'
                                                 '    if (x < w - 1) tryAdd(i + 1, x + 1, y);\n'
                                                 '    if (y > 0) tryAdd(i - w, x, y - 1);\n'
                                                 '    if (y < h - 1) tryAdd(i + w, x, y + 1);\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  let inRegion = 0;\n'
                                                 '  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) inRegion += region[i];\n'
                                                 '  wc.background_pct = Math.round(1000 * inRegion / N) / '
                                                 '10;\n'
                                                 "  if (wc.background_pct < 10) throw new Error('only ' + "
                                                 "wc.background_pct + '% of the image was found as "
                                                 'background connected to the border; nothing was '
                                                 "changed');\n"
                                                 '  // 4. The thin band around the fill (BAND px, 8 '
                                                 'neighbours per step), outside the box: these get the soft '
                                                 'curve. Only near-white, low\n'
                                                 '  //    colour pixels above the knee belong to it (the '
                                                 'faint edge of the shadow, soft background); a darker or '
                                                 'coloured pixel never does.\n'
                                                 '  const soft = j => { const hi = Math.max(R[j], G[j], '
                                                 'B[j]), lo = Math.min(R[j], G[j], B[j]); return lo > '
                                                 'kneeMin && hi - lo <= 30; };\n'
                                                 '  const ring = new Uint8Array(N);\n'
                                                 '  let front = region;\n'
                                                 '  for (let k = 0; k < BAND; k++) {\n'
                                                 '    const next = new Uint8Array(N);\n'
                                                 '    for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; '
                                                 'x++) {\n'
                                                 '      const i = y * w + x;\n'
                                                 '      if (!front[i]) continue;\n'
                                                 '      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) for (let dx = -1; '
                                                 'dx <= 1; dx++) {\n'
                                                 '        const xx = x + dx, yy = y + dy;\n'
                                                 '        if (xx < 0 || yy < 0 || xx >= w || yy >= h) '
                                                 'continue;\n'
                                                 '        const j = yy * w + xx;\n'
                                                 '        if (!region[j] && !ring[j] && !inBox(xx, yy) && '
                                                 'soft(j)) { ring[j] = 1; next[j] = 1; }\n'
                                                 '      }\n'
                                                 '    }\n'
                                                 '    front = next;\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  // 5. Write the picture. Every change is counted where '
                                                 'it happens: inside the box, and on pixels darker than the '
                                                 'knee.\n'
                                                 '  // Owner, 16 Oct 2026, 19:26 (Phase 1 question 3), the '
                                                 'fade is accepted on three conditions, each measured here:\n'
                                                 '  // (a) the fade stays within a small margin outside the '
                                                 'box (RAMP px): no pixel farther than RAMP from the box is '
                                                 'only partly changed;\n'
                                                 '  // (b) beyond that margin every background pixel is '
                                                 'exactly 255; (c) nothing inside the product box changes '
                                                 '(boxChanged, below).\n'
                                                 '  // 18h then checks the saved files for a grey halo.\n'
                                                 '  let changed = 0, ringChanged = 0, boxChanged = 0, '
                                                 'darkChanged = 0, white255After = 0, beyondNot255 = 0, '
                                                 'partialBeyond = 0, fadeMax = 0;\n'
                                                 '  const stride = Math.floor((24 * w + 31) / 32) * 4;\n'
                                                 '  const ob = Buffer.alloc(54 + stride * h);\n'
                                                 "  ob.write('BM', 0, 'latin1'); ob.writeUInt32LE(ob.length, "
                                                 '2); ob.writeUInt32LE(54, 10); ob.writeUInt32LE(40, 14);\n'
                                                 '  ob.writeInt32LE(w, 18); ob.writeInt32LE(h, 22); '
                                                 'ob.writeUInt16LE(1, 26); ob.writeUInt16LE(24, 28); '
                                                 'ob.writeUInt32LE(stride * h, 34);\n'
                                                 '  ob.writeInt32LE(2835, 38); ob.writeInt32LE(2835, 42);\n'
                                                 '  for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) {\n'
                                                 '    const obase = 54 + (h - 1 - y) * stride;\n'
                                                 '    for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) {\n'
                                                 '      const i = y * w + x;\n'
                                                 '      let r = R[i], g = G[i], bl = B[i];\n'
                                                 '      if (region[i] || ring[i]) {\n'
                                                 '        const wt = weight(x, y);\n'
                                                 '        const nr = Math.round(r + (lut[0][r] - r) * wt), '
                                                 'ng = Math.round(g + (lut[1][g] - g) * wt), nb = '
                                                 'Math.round(bl + (lut[2][bl] - bl) * wt);\n'
                                                 '        if (nr !== r || ng !== g || nb !== bl) {\n'
                                                 '          changed++;\n'
                                                 '          if (ring[i]) ringChanged++;\n'
                                                 '          if (inBox(x, y)) boxChanged++;\n'
                                                 '          if (Math.min(r, g, bl) <= kneeMin) '
                                                 'darkChanged++;\n'
                                                 '        }\n'
                                                 '        r = nr; g = ng; bl = nb;\n'
                                                 '        if (region[i] && r === 255 && g === 255 && bl === '
                                                 '255) white255After++;\n'
                                                 '        if (wt < 1 && wt > 0 && (nr !== R[i] || ng !== '
                                                 'G[i] || nb !== B[i])) { const dx = x < bx0 ? bx0 - x : (x '
                                                 '> bx1 ? x - bx1 : 0), dy = y < by0 ? by0 - y : (y > by1 ? '
                                                 'y - by1 : 0); const dd = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy); if '
                                                 '(dd > fadeMax) fadeMax = dd; if (dd > RAMP) '
                                                 'partialBeyond++; }\n'
                                                 '        if (region[i] && wt >= 1 && !(r === 255 && g === '
                                                 '255 && bl === 255)) beyondNot255++;\n'
                                                 '      }\n'
                                                 '      const q = obase + x * 3;\n'
                                                 '      ob[q] = bl; ob[q + 1] = g; ob[q + 2] = r;\n'
                                                 '    }\n'
                                                 '  }\n'
                                                 '  wc.pixels_changed_pct = Math.round(1000 * changed / N) / '
                                                 '10;\n'
                                                 '  wc.band_pixels_changed = ringChanged;\n'
                                                 '  wc.background_255_after_pct = inRegion ? Math.round(1000 '
                                                 '* white255After / inRegion) / 10 : 0;\n'
                                                 '  // Measured, not assumed (review finding 1): pixels '
                                                 'changed inside the product box, and pixels darker than the '
                                                 'knee that changed.\n'
                                                 '  wc.product_box_pixels_changed = boxChanged;\n'
                                                 '  wc.darker_than_knee_changed = darkChanged;\n'
                                                 '  wc.fade_margin_px = RAMP;\n'
                                                 '  wc.fade_reach_px = Math.round(fadeMax);\n'
                                                 '  wc.partly_changed_beyond_margin = partialBeyond;\n'
                                                 '  wc.background_beyond_margin_not_255 = beyondNot255;\n'
                                                 "  if (boxChanged || darkChanged) throw new Error('the "
                                                 "clean-up would have changed ' + boxChanged + ' pixels "
                                                 "inside the product box and ' + darkChanged + ' pixels "
                                                 "darker than the background; nothing was changed');\n"
                                                 "  if (partialBeyond || beyondNot255) throw new Error('the "
                                                 "fade reached past its ' + RAMP + ' px margin (' + "
                                                 "partialBeyond + ' pixels) or left ' + beyondNot255 + ' "
                                                 'background pixels beyond the margin below 255; nothing was '
                                                 "changed');\n"
                                                 '  wc.done = true; wc.cleaned = true;\n'
                                                 '  cleanBin = await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(ob, '
                                                 "pk.base + '_clean.bmp', 'image/bmp');\n"
                                                 '} catch (e) {\n'
                                                 '  if (e !== SKIP) { wc.done = false; wc.problem = '
                                                 'String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 300); }\n'
                                                 '}\n'
                                                 'pk.white_clean = wc;\n'
                                                 'if (wc.skipped) {\n'
                                                 '  // Packaged without the clean-up (owner, 19:26): pk.ok '
                                                 'stays as it was; the steps that need the box are listed as '
                                                 'skipped.\n'
                                                 '  pk.skipped_steps = (Array.isArray(pk.skipped_steps) ? '
                                                 'pk.skipped_steps : []).concat(wc.skipped_steps);\n'
                                                 "} else if (!wc.done) { pk.ok = false; pk.problem = 'The "
                                                 'package was not made: the background could not be set to '
                                                 "255 (' + wc.problem + '). The approved master is "
                                                 "unchanged. Nothing was uploaded.'; }\n"
                                                 'const out = { json: { pk } };\n'
                                                 'if (wc.done || wc.skipped) out.binary = { clean: cleanBin '
                                                 '};\n'
                                                 'return [out];'}},
