                                                 "'plant-large', 'clock', 'decor', 'bookend', 'box', "
                                                 "'serveware', 'dinnerware', 'glassware'],\n"
                                                 "        tabletop_ids: ['table-lamp', 'candle', 'vase', "
                                                 "'clock', 'decor', 'bookend', 'box', 'serveware', "
                                                 "'dinnerware', 'glassware'],\n"
                                                 "        room_scale_ids: ['sofa', 'recliner', 'chair', "
                                                 "'bench', 'dining', 'dining-table', 'centre-table', "
                                                 "'side-table', 'storage', 'bedroom', 'bed', 'mattress', "
                                                 "'rug', 'bedding', 'cushion', 'towel', 'robe', "
                                                 "'table-linen', 'bath', 'wall-art', 'mirror', 'screen', "
                                                 "'office-chair', 'office-desk', 'meeting', "
                                                 "'office-storage', 'outdoor', 'trolley'],\n"
                                                 "        room_rule_surface: 'level (0 degrees tilt), at the "
                                                 'height of the {surface} top the product will stand on plus '
                                                 "half the product\\'s height',\n"
                                                 "        room_rule_other: 'level, near the mid-height of "
                                                 "the product that will stand there',\n"
                                                 '        low_table_pattern: '
                                                 "'\\\\bon\\\\s+(?:top\\\\s+of\\\\s+)?(?:a|the)?\\\\s*(?:[a-z-]+\\\\s+){0,3}?(?:coffee|centre|center|cocktail|low)\\\\s+tables?\\\\b',\n"
                                                 '        table_pattern: '
                                                 "'\\\\bon\\\\s+(?:top\\\\s+of\\\\s+)?(?:a|the)?\\\\s*(?:[a-z-]+\\\\s+){0,3}?(?:tables?|consoles?|sideboards?|shelf|shelves|desks?|nightstands?|dressers?|mantel(?:piece)?|cabinets?|tv\\\\s+units?|counters?)\\\\b' "
                                                 '},\n'
                                                 '      // The empty room (no product in it yet).\n'
                                                 "      rules: 'Camera level: 0 degrees pitch, roll and yaw; "
                                                 'one-point perspective; vertical lines stay vertical; no '
                                                 "fisheye or wide-angle distortion.',\n"
                                                 '      // Camera views (owner, 16 Oct 2026, decision 24): 0 '
                                                 'degrees tilt for Full frontal, Left side, 45° right and '
                                                 'Right side. The Reference\n'
                                                 "      // view follows the vendor photo's perspective, as "
                                                 'the white master does. No fisheye in any case. "Left" and '
                                                 '"right" are as seen by a\n'
                                                 '      // person standing in front of the product, the same '
                                                 'as the handedness lines. View wording from the F1 Options '
                                                 'page (builder VIEW),\n'
                                                 '      // with A7 edits: the side lines carry the side gate '
                                                 'below, and "any side seating turns inward" is left out (A7 '
                                                 'keeps the arrangement of image 1).\n'
                                                 '      views: {\n'
                                                 "        'Reference view': 'The camera sees the product "
                                                 'from the same side, angle and perspective as image 1 (the '
                                                 'vendor photo); vertical lines stay vertical; no fisheye or '
                                                 "wide-angle distortion.',\n"
                                                 "        'Full frontal': 'A level camera facing the front "
                                                 'of the product at natural chest height, centred: 0 degrees '
                                                 'tilt, roll and yaw; one-point perspective; vertical lines '
                                                 "stay vertical; no fisheye or wide-angle distortion.',\n"
                                                 "        'Left side': 'The camera moves to the product\\'s "
                                                 'left side (as seen by a person standing in front of it) at '
                                                 'the same height: level, 0 degrees tilt and roll; vertical '
                                                 'lines stay vertical; no fisheye or wide-angle '
                                                 "distortion.',\n"
                                                 "        '45° right': 'The camera turns about 45 degrees to "
                                                 "the product\\'s right (as seen by a person standing in "
                                                 'front of it) at the same height: level, 0 degrees tilt and '
                                                 'roll; vertical lines stay vertical; no fisheye or '
                                                 "wide-angle distortion.',\n"
                                                 "        'Right side': 'The camera moves to the product\\'s "
                                                 'right side (as seen by a person standing in front of it) '
                                                 'at the same height: level, 0 degrees tilt and roll; '
                                                 'vertical lines stay vertical; no fisheye or wide-angle '
                                                 "distortion.'\n"
                                                 '      },\n'
                                                 '      // When the count cannot be read from chest height '
                                                 '(owner example: a 12-chair dining set), the camera may be '
                                                 'raised; the tilt stays 0.\n'
                                                 '      // min_pieces 9 (a table and 8 or more chairs) is an '
                                                 'ASSUMPTION; the owner named the 12-chair case only.\n'
                                                 '      // Owner, 16 Oct 2026 (D9): 9 pieces is a starting '
                                                 'rule; a 12-chair dining set goes into the first paid scene '
                                                 'test. If chair backs\n'
                                                 '      // are still hidden, a small downward tilt is '
                                                 'allowed for large dining sets only.\n'
                                                 "      raise: { families: ['dining'], min_pieces: 9, text: "
                                                 "'The camera may be raised above chest height so that every "
                                                 'piece stays countable; it stays level (0 degrees tilt) '
                                                 'with vertical lines vertical. Only if chair backs would '
                                                 'still hide pieces of this large dining set, a small '
                                                 'downward tilt of a few degrees is allowed, with vertical '
                                                 "lines kept as straight as possible.', basis: 'owner 16 Oct "
                                                 '2026 (decision 24; D9: a starting rule, to be checked on a '
                                                 "12-chair set)' }\n"
                                                 '    },\n'
                                                 '    // Light by colour temperature, not mood words (MI 6e, '
